        "abstract": "SUNBURST, a monitoring and communication network covering the US and Canada to alert electric utilities to the onset and magnitude of a solar magnetic disturbance (SMD), is discussed. Experience with a system involving data collection and local storage of information from multiple points at a substation, which was developed and field tested as part of a study concerned with the measurement of magnetic fields (EPRI Project RP2942-1), is briefly summarized. The design of SUNBURST is described.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
